          "html": "<p>Yesterday you learned the six decision areas. Today you learn the raw materials you make those decisions with — line, shape, form, space, texture, colour, value, type — and the dozen honest rules about how human eyes group and separate them. These rules are not decoration advice; they are perception. Once you know that things close together read as a group, you stop wondering why your five bullet points look like a random pile and start controlling the grouping on purpose.</p>\n<p>This is the day that separates people who \"have an eye\" from people who have vocabulary.</p>"
