          "html": "<ul><li><strong>Photo fundamentals:</strong> exposure triangle (aperture, shutter, ISO), white balance, and why phone cameras over-sharpen.</li><li><strong>Editing order of operations:</strong> crop and straighten → exposure → white balance → contrast → local adjustments → retouch → sharpen/export.</li><li><strong>Snapseed's core tools:</strong> Tune Image, Selective, Healing, Perspective, Details, Curves, White Balance, Expand.</li><li><strong>Photographing products on a phone:</strong> window light, bounce card, white backdrop, avoiding mixed lighting, using a second phone as a light.</li><li><strong>Background removal and compositing basics:</strong> layers, masks, blend modes (multiply for shadows, screen for glows).</li><li>Take <strong>three product photos</strong> of one object today (a shoe, a bottle, a phone) in three different lights. You'll edit them tomorrow.</li></ul>"
