          "id": "scenario",
          "title": "Scenario",
          "html": "<p><strong>Rescuing the restaurant photo.</strong> A small restaurant sends you one photo of their signature dish: shot at night with the phone torch, on a busy tablecloth, slightly blurred, with a menu and a phone visible at the edge, and their logo already burned into the corner. They want it for a Facebook post and a printed menu insert.</p>\n<p>You have 15 minutes and your phone. Produce a <strong>before/after pair</strong> plus a short note:</p>\n<ul><li>Crop to remove the distracting objects — and note what you lost.</li><li>Fix the colour cast from the torch, and get the food to look appetising (warm, saturated but not neon, with real texture).</li><li>Sharpen selectively so the food looks crisp but the background doesn't get noisy.</li><li>Decide whether to remove the burned-in logo (it's now in a bad position). If yes, how? If no, why not?</li><li>Flag honestly whether any of this should go to print, or whether the resolution limits it to screen. Give the pixel maths.</li></ul>\n<p>Then create a second version with the dish cut out onto a clean colour background — this is the version they'd use for a menu where photos need consistent backgrounds.</p>"
