          "html": "<ul><li><strong>Logo types:</strong> wordmark, lettermark/monogram, pictorial mark, abstract mark, mascot, emblem, combination mark. Find two real examples of each.</li><li><strong>Logo design process:</strong> brief → word associations → 50 rough sketches → shortlist → vector build → test at scale → hand-off.</li><li><strong>Visual tricks in marks:</strong> negative space, implied shapes (closure), monograms, geometric construction, dual meaning.</li><li><strong>Testing a logo:</strong> at 16 px, in one colour, reversed on dark, on a busy photo, at 5 m, and printed small.</li><li><strong>Vector basics:</strong> what a path, anchor point and bezier handle are — enough to understand why logos are drawn, not filtered.</li><li>Bring <strong>ten logo screenshots</strong> to Pinterest: five you think are excellent, five you think are weak. You'll argue why tomorrow.</li></ul>"
