          "html": "<ol><li><strong>(5 min) Word map.</strong> 20 words for your capstone brand. Circle the three that could be drawn.</li><li><strong>(10 min) Ten in two minutes.</strong> Ten thumbnails in 120 seconds, no judging. This breaks the \"I can't draw\" freeze.</li><li><strong>(25 min) Fifty.</strong> Keep going, two per minute. Include: wordmarks, monograms, geometric abstractions, and at least five bad jokes. Photograph the sheet — it goes in your portfolio process shots.</li><li><strong>(15 min) Shortlist three.</strong> For each, write one sentence: <em>\"This works because ___ and it will survive ___.\"</em> Cut the ones you can't defend.</li><li><strong>(20 min) Build one.</strong> In Canva, 1080×1080, build the shortlisted mark from primitives and type. Then tune: stroke weight consistency, gap sizes, optical centring, and the space between mark and name.</li><li><strong>(10 min) Test sheet.</strong> Run all seven tests. Fix the ones that fail. Save the sheet — you'll show it on Day 14.</li></ol>"
