          "html": "<ol><li><strong>(10 min) Lockups.</strong> Build horizontal, stacked and icon-only versions of your logo in Canva. Same weight, same spacing logic. Export all three.</li><li><strong>(10 min) Clear space.</strong> Choose your unit (cap height or the height of the icon), draw the dashed boundary, and place the logo at 1x on all sides. Screenshot for the sheet.</li><li><strong>(10 min) Minimum size.</strong> Shrink until it fails; record print and screen minimums. Include the 16 px and 32 px tests on the sheet.</li><li><strong>(10 min) Colour roles table.</strong> Write the five roles with hex codes and the approved text/background pairings, with contrast ratios. This table is the most-used part of any brand sheet.</li><li><strong>(10 min) Type system.</strong> Typeface, weights, three-size scale for print and screen, fallbacks, and two \"never\" rules.</li><li><strong>(15 min) Assemble the sheet.</strong> One A4 page, your grid from Day 6, three type sizes, restrained colour. It should look like a document, not a poster. Export as PDF.</li></ol>"
