          "id": "scenario",
          "title": "Scenario",
          "html": "<p><strong>The zero-budget laundry campaign.</strong> A laundry and dry-cleaning service near a university has a budget of nothing. No photographer, no studio, no models, no props beyond what exists. They want three images for Instagram that make students trust them with their good clothes, and they want to look \"cleaner and more careful than the place down the road\".</p>\n<p>Constraints: phone only, one afternoon, one shop, one member of staff willing to appear in one photo.</p>\n<p>Produce the campaign:</p>\n<ul><li>A single-minded proposition and a two-sentence concept statement.</li><li>A seven-rule shoot brief (light, colour, framing, density, props, gesture, crop).</li><li>Three images: establishing (the shop interior, folded stacks, or the counter), detail (fabric texture, a folded collar, a hanger), human (hands folding, a staff member at work — not posing).</li><li>A one-page rationale for the owner: what each image is doing, what it says about care, and why there's no \"before/after\" shot (because at this budget, a bad \"before\" photo would undermine trust rather than build it).</li><li>All three edited together, matched, and exported at 4:5.</li></ul>\n<p>This is a real portfolio piece. Treat the rationale as part of the deliverable — clients buy the thinking.</p>"
