          "html": "<p><strong>\"A few small changes.\"</strong> You delivered a logo, brand sheet and a flyer for a client two weeks ago. They paid the 50% deposit but not the balance. Now they message:</p>\n<blockquote><p>\"Looks good! Just a few small changes — can we try a different colour blue, a different font for the logo, change the icon to a shopping basket, add a tagline, and also make a version for our t-shirts, banners, and a 30-second video? Should be quick since you have the files. Also my brother says the logo looks like our competitor's, so maybe start the logo again but keep everything else. We need it all by Friday.\"</p></blockquote>\n<p>Produce, in under 300 words:</p>\n<ul><li>A reply that keeps the relationship and protects the work: acknowledge, then separate what's included, what's new work, and what's a different project.</li><li>A <strong>change order</strong> with three line items and prices, using your rate card.</li><li>A note about the unpaid balance, raised without apology.</li><li>The new timeline, based on real capacity rather than their deadline.</li><li>One sentence on the \"looks like our competitor\" claim: how you'd verify it (put them side by side at thumbnail size) before agreeing to a redesign.</li></ul>\n<p>Write this as the actual message you'd send. It is the most valuable 300 words in the course.</p>"
