        "title": "10. Contrast quick reference",
        "html": "<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Text</th><th>Minimum ratio</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Body text</td><td>4.5 : 1</td><td>Anything you expect people to read in full</td></tr><tr><td>Large text (24 px+, or 19 px bold+)</td><td>3 : 1</td><td>Headlines</td></tr><tr><td>Icons and UI boundaries</td><td>3 : 1</td><td>Buttons, form outlines</td></tr><tr><td>Decorative</td><td>No minimum</td><td>If it carries no meaning, it's exempt — but be honest about what's decorative</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Test at webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker. Grey (#999) on white is 2.85:1 — the single most common accessibility failure in amateur design.</p>"
